# jemdoc: menu{menu-lab.jemdoc}{lab.html}, title{Lab}, notime
The Edge AI Lab studies the algorithms behind networked intelligence: how
computation is split between a device and the edge, how learning survives when
data cannot be pooled, and how the network underneath decides what is possible.
Our work sits at the intersection of machine learning, communication and
optimization, and we are most interested in problems where computation,
bandwidth and privacy are all scarce at the same time.

We are part of the School of Computer Science and Engineering at International
University, Vietnam National University Ho Chi Minh City. See
[lab-members.html Members] for the people behind the work.

== What we work on

- Semantic communication and edge intelligence
- Time series analysis and forecasting
- Federated and distributed learning under limited communication
- Deep reinforcement learning for network control
- Resource allocation, caching and adaptive streaming
- Optimization and game theory for shared resources

== Join us

We welcome both *undergraduate* and *graduate* students. You do not need to
have worked on all of the topics above -- what matters is that you are willing
to read papers carefully, write code, and stay with a problem long enough to
find out whether it is actually hard.

If you are interested, email [mailto:YOUR_EMAIL YOUR_EMAIL] with a short note
about what you would like to work on.

